cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Label-Free Reliability Test for FR-I/FR-II Classification
  in Blind Radio Surveys
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both
  the software (this record) and the Research Note it
  supports.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kondekar
    given-names: Raj
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8798-2540"
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/astrophile73/radio-astronomy-ml-morphology
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registered analysis record and results for a study
  of how a MiraBest-trained FR-I/FR-II classifier behaves when
  applied to a blind sample of FIRST catalogue components.
  Predicted class changes under a rotation or mirror for 21.7
  per cent of candidates, against 11.4 per cent for MiraBest
  sources held out under five-fold cross-validation.
  Restricting candidates to MiraBest's angular-size range, or
  to isolated components, does not recover stability.
keywords:
  - radio astronomy
  - radio galaxies
  - Fanaroff-Riley classification
  - FIRST survey
  - MiraBest
  - domain shift
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - convolutional neural networks
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
# date-released is the date this version was released, not the date
# work began. Set it to the day you tag v1.0.0 and publish the Zenodo
# record. See research/DECISIONS.md for the project timeline.
date-released: "2026-11-24"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24497097"
